<h1>Miracle Sort</h1>
<p>
    Miracle Sort begins by checking if the array is sorted.
    If it is not it stops and waits for a miracle to sort the array,
    such as another program sorting the array 
    or cosmic rays or a computer bug
    changing the values in the array so that it becomes sorted.
    After waiting, Miracle Sort again checks if the array is sorted.
    It repeats this process until a miracle sorts the array, 
    or more likely until the user stops it and uses a better sorting algorithm.
</p>

